Description: Constructs and analyzes networks from pairwise mutual information.
    Variables are discretized using the Freedman-Diaconis or Sturges rule,
    and mutual information is estimated using a plug-in estimator and
    normalized by joint entropy. Indirect links can be pruned using the
    data processing inequality. The package includes shuffled-data
    generation for null distributions, network topology and path
    statistics, GEXF export, and disk-backed batch and parallel
    computation for large datasets.
